    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does LinkedIn lead generation work for Real Estate Developers + Brokers?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">5 mechanisms combined: (1) Sales Navigator search + list building — target HNI investors + institutional tenants + REIT-fund managers + industry associations (CREDAI/NAREDCO) + policy makers. (2) Personalized connection + InMail sequences (proven templates + industry-native writing). (3) Content-led inbound — regular posts + articles + newsletter drive brand-recall + inbound DMs. (4) LinkedIn Ads (Sponsored Content + Message Ads + Conversation Ads + Lead Gen Forms) for scale. (5) WhatsApp handoff + CRM integration — qualified leads flow to your sales team within 5-15 minutes. For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager, well-executed LinkedIn drives 1 senior developer or broker retained on LinkedIn drives Rs 10-100 crore in project-attributed leasing + investment inflow.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How many qualified leads should we expect from LinkedIn per month?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager at Growth+ package tier, well-executed month 6-12: 20-80 qualified DMs/month, 3-15 booked meetings/month, 1-5 closed opportunities/month attributable to LinkedIn. Month 12-24: 40-200 qualified DMs, 8-30 booked meetings, 3-10 closed opportunities. Month 24+: compounding — LinkedIn becomes primary top-of-funnel channel for many Real Estate Developers + Brokers.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is Sales Navigator + how much does it cost?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">LinkedIn Sales Navigator is a premium lead-search tool: Rs 4,000-8,000/month per seat (Core plan) OR Rs 8,000-14,000/month (Advanced plan with team features). Capabilities: advanced ICP search (filter by role + industry + geography + seniority + company size + tech-stack + recent job change + intent signals), lead + account lists, InMail credits, TeamLink (warm intros via team's connections), saved searches with alerts. For Real Estate Developers + Brokers targeting HNI investors + institutional tenants + REIT-fund managers + industry associations (CREDAI/NAREDCO) + policy makers, Sales Nav is ROI-positive from month 2 onwards. ITD manages Sales Navigator as part of Premium + Enterprise tiers.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do personalized InMail sequences work?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Sequence: (1) Sales Nav filters build target list (200-500 leads matching ICP). (2) Personalized connection request — 200 chars, mentions specific context (their recent post, their firm's news, mutual connection). (3) Wait 3-5 days post-connection — engage with their content (like + comment on their posts). (4) First InMail with value-first framing — industry insight, specific relevance to their business, offer of resource. (5) 7-14 day follow-up with a resource or insight. (6) 30-day nurture with content sharing + relationship-building. Response rate: 15-35% for well-crafted sequences (vs 2-8% for generic mass-outreach).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What LinkedIn Ads formats work for Real Estate Developers + Brokers?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) Sponsored Content (native feed ads) — text + image or video, best for awareness + engagement (Rs 40-200 CPL for Real Estate Developers + Brokers). (2) Message Ads (direct message to target inbox) — 20-40% open rate, best for high-value outreach (Rs 200-1,500 per response). (3) Conversation Ads (interactive branching-message ads) — 3-5x engagement vs static Message Ads. (4) Lead Gen Forms (auto-fill from LinkedIn profile) — best for high-volume qualified inbound. (5) Document Ads (PDF delivered in-feed) — best for whitepaper + report distribution. For Real Estate Developers + Brokers, recommended mix: 40-50% Sponsored Content + 25-30% Message Ads + 15-20% Conversation Ads + 10-15% Lead Gen Forms.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we integrate LinkedIn leads with our CRM?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">3-step handoff: (1) LinkedIn leads flow to CRM (HubSpot/Salesforce/Zoho) with source-tag + LinkedIn profile context via Zapier or LinkedIn Marketing Solutions API. (2) Lead scoring (BANT + fit + engagement signal) auto-assigns Marketing-Qualified vs Sales-Qualified status. (3) SQL leads route to sales rep with LinkedIn context + suggested talking points + engagement history. Response SLA: 5-15 minutes for hot leads. Weekly lead-quality review + monthly cohort-conversion analysis with your sales team.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does WhatsApp CTWA (Click-to-WhatsApp) work with LinkedIn?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Two paths: (1) LinkedIn content includes WhatsApp CTA in About Us + Featured section + comments — driven by LinkedIn-attributed traffic + trackable via UTM. (2) LinkedIn DM handoff — qualified DM inbounds transition to WhatsApp for faster response + inside-sales follow-up. For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager where buyers are 40+ (banking, real estate, manufacturing, senior consulting), WhatsApp is often preferred over email for initial outreach — 60-80% open rate vs 25% for email.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we handle inbound LinkedIn DMs at scale?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">For Developer, MD/CEO of real estate firm, Commercial Property Broker (CBRE/JLL/Colliers-tier), REIT founder, Real Estate Fund Manager generating 20-100+ DMs/month, DM handling workflow: (1) Auto-response acknowledging inbound (within 5 min). (2) Qualifying questions (concern + timeline + budget + geography). (3) Route qualified to WhatsApp/email/Calendly (15-min SLA business hours). (4) Route unqualified to newsletter subscribe or content resource. (5) Weekly DM analytics: volume + response time + qualified-lead rate + conversion. ITD's Growth + Premium tiers include DM handling with 15-min SLA.</div>
